---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Infrastructure Funds | Platizio Alternatives" currentPage="products/funds/infrastructure">

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-8 lg:max-w-5xl">

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-secondary mb-8 pt-4">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif" class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-label hover:text-primary-container transition-colors">AIF Knowledge</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[12px]">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-label text-secondary">Cat I AIF</span>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[12px]">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-label text-on-surface">Infrastructure Funds</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
      <span class="bg-secondary/10 text-secondary text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1">Category I AIF</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-headline text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light leading-tight text-primary-container mb-4">
      Infrastructure <span class="italic">Funds</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed text-lg max-w-2xl">
      Financing the arteries of economic growth through long-duration capital commitments in regulated, essential-service assets with contractual yield profiles.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Definition & Purpose -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-8 md:p-10 relative overflow-hidden">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl mb-6 text-primary-container">Definition & Purpose</h2>
      <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Infrastructure Funds under Category I AIF channel institutional capital into essential public-service assets—roads, ports, airports, power transmission networks, renewable energy installations, and urban utilities. These assets are characterized by long operating lives, regulated tariff structures, and contractual cash flows that provide a natural match for patient institutional capital. SEBI's Category I designation reflects the government's policy intent to channel private capital into infrastructure formation, recognizing the sector's multiplier effect on broader economic productivity.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">apartment</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Focus</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Long-term Infrastructure</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">monitoring</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Risk Profile</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Moderate–High</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">payments</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Min. Investment</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">&#8377;1 Crore</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">schedule</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Tenure</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">10–15 Years</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Characteristics -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-10 text-primary-container pl-4 border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed">
      Key <span class="italic">Characteristics</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">policy</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Regulated Asset Base</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Infrastructure assets operate under concession agreements, power purchase agreements, or regulatory tariff orders that define allowable revenue for extended periods—often 25 to 30 years. This contractual revenue certainty reduces cash flow volatility to near-sovereign levels, making infrastructure returns more predictable than virtually any other alternative asset class.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">hourglass_bottom</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Long Tenure Capital Deployment</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Fund lifecycles of 10 to 15 years match the development, construction, and stabilization phases of large infrastructure projects. Patient capital is rewarded with illiquidity premia of 200 to 400 basis points above listed market equivalents. Evergreen structures and InvIT listings provide secondary liquidity mechanisms once assets achieve operational maturity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">savings</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Steady Yield Distribution</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Operational infrastructure assets generate predictable dividend or distribution streams linked to toll revenues, capacity charges, or annuity payments from government counterparties. Fund structures often incorporate waterfall distributions that prioritize investor return of capital and preferred return before carry is earned—aligning manager incentives with investor outcomes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lifecycle -->
  <section class="mb-16 bg-primary-container p-8 md:p-12 overflow-hidden relative">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-12 text-tertiary-fixed">The Infrastructure Fund <span class="italic">Lifecycle</span></h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div>
        <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Phase 01</div>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-3">Development & Acquisition</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Fund managers source assets through government tender processes, bilateral negotiations with infrastructure developers, or secondary market acquisitions of operational concessions. Greenfield investments carry construction and demand risk premiums; brownfield acquisitions offer de-risked cash flows at higher entry multiples.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Phase 02</div>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-3">Construction & Ramp-Up</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">The construction phase involves capital call drawdowns, engineering oversight, regulatory milestone management, and debt financing optimization. Experienced managers deploy dedicated project management teams to track cost overruns, construction timelines, and environmental compliance—protecting the fund's equity position through commissioning.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Phase 03</div>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-3">Operations & Exit</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Operational assets generate recurring yield distributed to LPs annually or semi-annually. Exit is achieved through listing as an InvIT or Infrastructure Holding Company, strategic sale to a sovereign wealth fund or pension, or refinancing and recapitalization that returns equity capital while retaining fee-generating asset management mandates.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Notable Benchmarks -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-8 text-primary-container">Institutional <span class="italic">Benchmarks</span></h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">NIIF (National Investment and Infrastructure Fund)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-3">Sovereign Infrastructure Platform</p>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">India's quasi-sovereign infrastructure investment platform, NIIF operates a Master Fund, Fund of Funds, and Strategic Opportunities Fund. With a target corpus exceeding $4 billion and sovereign co-investment from Abu Dhabi Investment Authority, Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan, and other global LPs, NIIF represents the highest tier of institutional infrastructure investment in the Indian market.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">India Infrastructure Fund</h3>
        <p class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-3">3i-Managed Core Infrastructure Vehicle</p>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Managed by 3i India Infrastructure, this fund targets operational or near-operational infrastructure assets across energy, transport, and utilities in India. Its portfolio includes investments in road concessions, port terminals, and renewable energy projects, providing investors exposure to a diversified stream of long-duration contractual cash flows with defined inflation linkage through indexed tariff structures.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <div class="bg-surface-container p-8 text-center border border-outline-variant/10">
    <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl mb-4 text-on-surface">Explore This Strategy</h3>
    <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm mb-8">Access detailed regulatory filings and performance metrics through our private concierge.</p>
    <a href="/partner" class="inline-block w-full md:w-auto py-4 px-10 bg-primary-container text-on-primary font-label text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] hover:bg-slate-800 transition-colors">
      Request Fund Prospectus
    </a>
  </div>

</div>

</BaseLayout>
